        "galleryLabels": [
          {
            "text": "Standing Krishna\r\n500–600 AD\r\nThe tight hair curls and the three chignons of this figure may\r\nindicate that it represents Krishna, one of the manifestations\r\nof Vishnu. The three twists of hair would therefore symbolise\r\nVishnu’s three cosmic strides (trivikrama). Krishna appears to\r\nhave played a central role in pre-Angkorian Cambodia but very\r\nfew images of him survive.\r\nSandstone\r\nCambodia\r\nIn memory of Anthony Gardner. A gift from the beneficiaries of the\r\nAnthony Gardner estate\r\nMuseum no. IS.88-1993",
